91 \\times 6) \\times 10\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\(91 \\times 6\\):\n\\[\n91 \\times 6 = (90 + 1) \\times 6 = (90 \\times 6) + (1 \\times 6) = 540 + 6 = 546\n\\]\n\nThen multiply by 10:\n\\[\n546 \\times 10 = 5,\\!460\n\\]\n\n**Verification using the distributive property:**\n\\[\n91 \\times 60 = (90 + 1) \\times 60 = (90 \\times 60) + (1 \\times 60) = 5,\\!400 + 60 = 5,\\!460\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the result. \n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{5460}\\)",
