ee, 25 is 20 + 5. So (20 +5)*36 = 20*36 +5*36. Let's calculate that. 20*36 is 720, and 5*36 is 180. Adding those together: 720 + 180 = 900. Yep, same result.\n\nWait, maybe even another method. Since 25*4=100, so if I can get a 4 from 36. Let me see. 36 divided by 4 is 9. So 25*(4*9) = 25*4*9 = 100*9 = 900. Oh, that's clever. That works too. So that's another way to see it.\n\nAll these different methods are leading me to 900. I think that must be the correct answer then. Let me just confirm with a calculator in my mind. 25 times 36. 25*30 is 750, plus 25*6 is 150, so 750+150 is definitely 900. Yeah, that checks out. I don't think I made any mistakes here. So the product of 25 and 36 is 900.\n"]
