is four digits: 2 (thousands), 0 (hundreds), 7 (tens), 0 (units). \n\nSo aligning:\n\n\u2003\u00a0115\n\n+2070\n\n------\n\nStart from the right:\n\nUnits: 5 +0 =5\n\nTens: 1 +7=8\n\nHundreds: 1 +0=1\n\nThousands: 0 +2=2\n\nSo total is 2185. Okay, that seems consistent.\n\nWait, but let me check using another method to confirm. Maybe using the difference of squares or another approach?\n\nAlternatively, perhaps 23 \u00d7 95 can be thought of as (20 + 3)(90 +5). But that might complicate. Alternatively, 95 is 100 -5. So 23\u00d7(100-5)=23\u00d7100 -23\u00d75=2300 -115=2185. Oh, that's another way and gives the same result. That confirms it again.\n\nSo 23\u00d7100 is 2300, minus 23\u00d75=115, so 2300-115=2185. Yep, that works. So that's another method and same answer. So I think that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do 23\u00d795 as 23\u00d7(9\u00d710 +5). But that's similar to before. Anyway, seems like all methods point to 2185. Wait, but let me check with straight multiplication:\n\n23\n\ntimes 95. Let's do 23\u00d75 first: 115. Then 23\u00d790: 23\u00d79=207, so 2070. Adding those gives 2185. Okay, that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, if I use the standard multiplication:\n\n\u2003\u2003\u00a023\n\n\u00d7\u00a095\n\n--------\n\nFirst step: 23\u00d75=115\n\nSecond step: 23\u00d790=2070\n\nAdd them together: 115 +2070=2185.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can use a calculator, but since this is a thought process, I have to do it manually. Let me see if there's any chance I messed up a multiplication step.\n\nWait, 23\u00d79: 20\u00d79=180, 3\u00d79=27. 180+27=207. So that's correct. Then times 10 is 2070. Then adding 115: yes, 2070 +100 is 2170, plus 15 is 2185.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do 95\u00d720 and 95\u00d73, then add. Let's see:\n\n95\u00d720: 95\u00d72=190, so times 10 is 1900.\n\n95\u00d73: 285.\n\nAdding 1900 +285 =2185. Yep, that works too. So that's another way. So that's consistent again.\n\nHmm, so all methods lead to 2185. Therefore, the product of 23 and 95 is 2185. I think that's the correct answer. I don't see any errors in my calculations, and cross-verifying with different methods gives the same result. So I'm confident that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 23 and 95 is \\boxed{2185}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 23 and 95, we can use the distributive property and the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nFirst, we break down the multiplication using the distributive property:\n\\[\n23 \\times 95 = 23 \\times (90 + 5) = (23 \\times 90) + (23 \\times 5)\n\\]\n\nCalculating each part separately:\n1. \\(23 \\times 5\\):\n   \\[\n   23 \\times 5 = 115\n   \\]\n\n2. \\(23 \\times 90\\):\n   \\[\n   23 \\times 90 = 23 \\times (9 \\times 10) = (23 \\times 9) \\times 10\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   23 \\times 9 = 207 \\quad \\text{(since } 20 \\times 9 = 180 \\text{ and } 3 \\times 9 = 27; 180 + 27 = 207\\text{)}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   207 \\times 10 = 2070\n   \\]\n\nAdding the two results together:\n\\[\n115 + 2070 = 2185\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify this using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n   \\quad 23 \\\\\n\\times 95 \\\\\n\\hline\n   115 \\quad (\\text{23 \u00d7 5}) \\\\\n+2070 \\quad (\\text{23 \u00d7 90, shifted one position to the left}) \\\\\n\\hline\n   2185 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 23 and 95 is \\(\\boxed{2185}\\).",
