 first.\n\n2100 + 210 is 2310. Then 70 +7 is 77. So 2310 +77 is 2387. Yeah, same result. Okay that seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do it another way to cross-verify. Let me try the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nMultiplying 77 by 31. Let's write it as:\n\n\u2003\u200377  \n× 31  \n—————  \nFirst, multiply 77 by 1 (the units place of 31), which is 77.  \nThen multiply 77 by 30 (the tens place of 31). So 77 × 30. Well, 77×3 is 231, so times 10 is 2310.  \nNow add the two results: 77 + 2310. Let's see, 2310 + 70 is 2380, plus 7 more is 2387. Same answer again. Okay, that's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method, like the difference of squares or some other trick? Let me see. Hmm, 77 and 31... Not sure if they fit into a difference of squares, but maybe another approach.\n\nAlternatively, note that 77 is 7×11 and 31 is a prime number. But I don't think that helps directly. Maybe just multiply straight out. \n\nAlternatively, think of 31 as 30 +1, so 77×30 +77×1. Wait, that's exactly what I did before, so same result.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps 77×31. Let me reverse it, 31×70 is 2170, and 31×7 is 217. Then add them together: 2170 +217. Let me compute that: 2170 +200 is 2370, plus 17 is 2387. Yep, same answer again.\n\nHmm, so all methods are leading me to 2387. I think that's the correct product. Let me just confirm with a calculator in my mind. Wait, 77×30 is 2310, plus 77 gives 2387. Yeah, that seems right. I don't see any errors in the steps. So I think the answer is 2387.\n"]
