735 first. 70 times 35. Well, 70\u00d730 is 2100, and 70\u00d75 is 350. So 2100 +350 is 2450.\n\nThen 8\u00d735 is 280. Adding those together: 2450 +280 = 2730. Okay, that matches the previous result. Good, so that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking down 35 into 30 +5. Wait, that's similar to what I just did. Hmm. Alternatively, maybe using some other method like the lattice method, but that might be overcomplicating.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the fact that 78\u00d735 is the same as 78\u00d7(30+5) which we did. Or even 35\u00d778. Let me try another approach to confirm once more.\n\nLet me do 35\u00d770 and 35\u00d78. Wait, that might not help. Alternatively, 78\u00d735. Let me think in terms of 78 multiplied by 35. Maybe converting into easier numbers. For instance, 78\u00d735 is the same as 78\u00d7(35). Hmm, perhaps 78\u00d735 = (80 -2) \u00d735. Let's see:\n\n(80 -2) \u00d735 = 80\u00d735 - 2\u00d735. \n\nCalculating 80\u00d735: 80\u00d730=2400, 80\u00d75=400, so total is 2400 +400=2800. Then subtract 2\u00d735=70. So 2800 -70=2730. \n\nAgain, same result. So that's three different methods all leading to 2730. That gives me confidence that the answer is correct. \n\nWait, but just to be thorough, maybe I can do straight multiplication again. Let me try the vertical method once more.\n\n   78\n\u00d7 35\n------\nFirst multiply by 5 (the ones place):\n\n5\u00d78=40, write 0 carryover 4.\n\n5\u00d77=35 +4=39, so first partial product is 390.\n\nThen multiply by 3 (the tens place, so actually 30). But when writing vertically, you shift one position to the left.\n\nSo:\n\n3\u00d78=24, write down 4, carryover 2.\n\n3\u00d77=21 +2=23. So that gives 234, but since it's the tens place, it's 2340.\n\nAdding 390 +2340:\n\n2340 + 390. Let's do 2340 + 300 =2640, then +90 is 2730. Yep, same result.\n\nAlright, so all methods are giving me 2730. I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. Maybe one last check with a calculator method? Well, since I can't use a calculator, but let me do 78\u00d735 step by step once again.\n\nAlternatively, think of 35 as 7\u00d75, so 78\u00d77\u00d75. Let's see:\n\n78\u00d77: 70\u00d77=490, 8\u00d77=56, so 490+56=546. Then 546\u00d75. \n\n546\u00d75: 500\u00d75=2500, 40\u00d75=200, 6\u00d75=30. So 2500+200=2700, +30=2730. \n\nSame answer again. Wow, that's four different methods all leading to the same result. I think that's pretty conclusive. \n\nTherefore, the product of 78 and 35 is 2730.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 78 and 35 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Breakdown using distributive property:**\n   - \\(78 \\times 35 = (70 + 8) \\times 35\\)\n   - \\(= 70 \\times 35 + 8 \\times 35\\)\n   - \\(= 2450 + 280 = 2730\\)\n\n2. **Standard vertical multiplication:**\n   - Multiply 78 by 5: \\(78 \\times 5 = 390\\)\n   - Multiply 78 by 30 (shifted one position left): \\(78 \\times 30 = 2340\\)\n   - Add results: \\(390 + 2340 = 2730\\)\n\n3. **Alternative method using \\( (80 - 2) \\times 35 \\):**\n   - \\(80 \\times 35 = 2800\\)\n   - Subtract \\(2 \\times 35 = 70\\)\n   - \\(2800 - 70 = 2730\\)\n\n4. **Verification via component multiplication:**\n   - \\(78 \\times 7 = 546\\), then \\(546 \\times 5 = 2730\\)\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent.\n\n**Answer:** \\boxed{2730}",
