28, then times 11. 128*11. To multiply by 11, you can do 128*10 + 128 = 1280 + 128 = 1408. That works too. \n\nAlternatively, maybe 32 is 16*2, so 44*16*2. 44*2 is 88, so 88*16. Hmm, 88*10 is 880, 88*6 is 528, so 880+528=1408. \n\nAll methods lead to 1408, so that must be the correct answer. Let me just confirm with a calculator in my mind. 44 times 30 is 1320, plus 44 times 2 is 88, so 1320 +88 is 1408. Yep, that's solid. I think that's the product.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 44 and 32 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Break down using distributive property**:\n   \\[\n   44 \\times 32 = 44 \\times (30 + 2)\n   \\]\n2. **Multiply each term separately**:\n   \\[\n   44 \\times 30 = 1,\\!320 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 44 \\times 2 = 88\n   \\]\n3. **Add the results**:\n   \\[\n   1,\\!320 + 88 = 1,\\!408\n   \\]\n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{1408}\\)",
