60. Adding those together gives 750 + 60 = 810. Same answer again. Good, that's consistent.\n\nWait, maybe I can use another approach just to confirm. Let's think in terms of hundreds. 30 times 30 would be 900, right? But since it's 27 instead of 30, that's 3 less. So 30 times 3 is 90, so subtracting that from 900 would be 900 - 90 = 810. Oh, that works too. So that also gives me 810. \n\nHmm, all the different methods are pointing to 810. I think that's the right answer. Let me just do the straight multiplication once more to be 100% sure. \n\n27 multiplied by 30. Since 30 has a zero in the ones place and 3 in the tens, when you multiply 27 by 30, you can consider it as 27*3*10. 27*3 is 81, then times 10 is 810. Yep, that's the same as before. \n\nAlright, I think I've checked it enough ways. The product of 30 and 27 is definitely 810.\n"]
