2940, 80+18 is 98, so 2940+98=3038. \n\nSame result. \n\nI think that's thorough enough. All methods converge to 3038. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. So the product of 62 and 49 is 3038.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 62 and 49 can be calculated using the distributive property or standard multiplication. Here's a concise breakdown:\n\n**Method 1: Standard Algorithm**\n```\n    62\n  \u00d7 49\n  -----\n    558  (62 \u00d7 9)\n  +2480  (62 \u00d7 40, shifted left)\n  -----\n   3038\n```\n\n**Method 2: Distributive Property**\n\\[\n(60 + 2)(40 + 9) = 60\u00d740 + 60\u00d79 + 2\u00d740 + 2\u00d79 = 2400 + 540 + 80 + 18 = 3038\n\\]\n\n**Method 3: Simplified Calculation**\n\\[\n62 \u00d7 49 = 62 \u00d7 (50 - 1) = 62\u00d750 - 62 = 3100 - 62 = 3038\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 62 and 49 is \\boxed{3038}.",
