is the same as 32 squared minus something? Wait, 32 squared is 1024, but that might not help here. Alternatively, maybe (30 + 2)(20 + 2). Let me try expanding that. \n\nExpanding (30 + 2)(20 + 2) using FOIL:\nFirst: 30*20 = 600\nOuter: 30*2 = 60\nInner: 2*20 = 40\nLast: 2*2 = 4\nAdding those together: 600 + 60 is 660, plus 40 is 700, plus 4 is 704. So that also gives 704. \n\nOkay, so all methods are pointing to 704. Maybe I can check with a calculator if I have one, but since I'm doing this manually, I need to ensure I didn't make an arithmetic error. Let me do the multiplication step by step again.\n\n32 multiplied by 22. Let's write it out vertically:\n\n   32\nx 22\n-----\nFirst step: Multiply 32 by 2 (the ones digit of 22). 2*2 is 4, 2*30 is 60, so 64. \n\nSecond step: Multiply 32 by 20 (the tens digit, so shifted one position to the left). 20*2 is 40, and 20*30 is 600. So 640. \n\nAdding 64 and 640: 64 + 640. 64 + 600 is 664, plus 40 more? Wait, no, that's not right. Wait, no, 640 is 600 + 40, so adding 64 (which is 60 +4) gives 600+40+60+4. 600 + (40+60) is 600+100=700, plus 4 is 704. Yes, that works. \n\nHmm, maybe I confused myself for a moment there, but seems correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the fact that 22 is 11*2, so 32*11*2. 32*11 is 352, then times 2 is 704. That works too. \n\nWait, 32*11. 32*10 is 320, plus 32 is 352. Then 352*2 is 704. Yep, same answer. \n\nSo, all different methods lead me to 704. Therefore, I think the product of 32 and 22 is 704. I can't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I'm confident that's the right answer.\n"] 25%|██▌       | 125/500 [2:23:06<6:30:52, 62.54s/it]
