lations. Let me just do a quick estimate to check if it's reasonable. 67 is close to 70, so 70 times 70 is 4900. Since 67 is 3 less than 70, the actual product should be 3*70 = 210 less than 4900. So 4900 - 210 is 4690. Exactly! That matches. \n\nOkay, that's a good check. So the answer must be 4690.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 67 and 70 is calculated as follows:\n\nFirst, multiply 67 by 7:\n\\[\n67 \\times 7 = 469\n\\]\nThen, multiply the result by 10 (since 70 = 7 \\times 10):\n\\[\n469 \\times 10 = 4,\\!690\n\\]\n\n**Verification using the distributive property:**\n\\[\n(60 + 7) \\times 70 = 60 \\times 70 + 7 \\times 70 = 4,\\!200 + 490 = 4,\\!690\n\\]\n\n**Estimation check:**\n- \\(70 \\times 70 = 4,\\!900\\)\n- Subtract \\(3 \\times 70 = 210\\) (since 67 is 3 less than 70):\n\\[\n4,\\!900 - 210 = 4,\\!690\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:** \\(\\boxed{4690}\\)",
