ifting one place gives 4690. That matches my previous result. Okay, that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property another way. Let's see, 67 is 60 +7, and 70 is 70. So (60 +7)*70 = 60*70 +7*70. \n\nCalculating 60*70: 60 times 70. Well, 6*7 is 42, and then there are two zeros, so 4200. Then 7*70 is 490. Adding those together: 4200 + 490. Let's see, 4200 + 400 is 4600, then plus 90 is 4690. Yep, same answer again.\n\nHmm, all methods are giving me 4690, so I think that's the right answer. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. Let me just do a quick estimate to check if it's reasonable. 67 is close to 70, so 70 times 70 is 4900. Since 67 is 3 less than 70, the actual product should be 3*70 = 210 less than 4900. So 4900 - 210 is 4690. Exactly! That matches. \n\nOkay, that's a good check. So the answer must be 4690.\n"] 26%|██▌       | 131/500 [2:28:57<5:11:00, 50.57s/it]
