 down:\n\n\u2003\xa094\n×18\n------\nFirst multiply 94 by 8: which we already did as 752.\n\nThen multiply 94 by 10 (since the 1 in 18 is in the tens place, so it's actually 10). So 94 × 10 = 940. Then add the two results: 752 + 940. Wait, that's the same as before, so 1692 again. Okay, that's consistent.\n\nHmm, another way to check could be using another decomposition. Maybe 94 × 18 = (90 + 4) × 18. Let's see:\n\n90 × 18 + 4 × 18.\n\nCalculating 90 × 18: 90 × 10 = 900, 90 × 8 = 720, so 900 + 720 = 1620.\n\nThen 4 × 18 = 72. Adding those together: 1620 + 72 = 1692. Same answer again. Good, so that's three different methods all leading to 1692. I think that's solid.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using some other trick, like 18 is 20 - 2. So 94 × (20 - 2) = 94×20 - 94×2.\n\nCalculating 94 × 20: 94 × 2 = 188, so times 10 is 1880.\n\nThen subtract 94 ×2 which is 188. So 1880 - 188 = ?\n\nLet's do that subtraction: 1880 - 100 is 1780, then subtract 88 more: 1780 - 88 = 1692. Yep, same result. So that's a fourth method. Definitely, 1692 is the right answer.\n\nI guess there's no doubt here. All methods converge to 1692. So the product of 94 and 18 is 1692. I think that's it. Just to be thorough, maybe do the multiplication straight up:\n\n   94\n×18\n------\nMultiply 4 × 8 = 32, write down 2 carryover 3. Then 9×8=72 +3 =75, so write 75. So first line is 752.\n\nThen, next line, since it's the tens place, we start with a zero. 4×1=4, but shifted one position: so 4×10=40, but actually, it's 94×10, so 940. Then adding 752 + 940 as before. Yep, same steps.\n\nYep, all checks out. Confident that 1692 is correct.\n"] 38%|███▊      | 191/500 [3:31:07<5:23:18, 62.78s/it]
