      "text": ":\nOkay, let me try to figure out the product of 77 and 36. Hmm, multiplication, right? So I need to multiply these two numbers together. Let me recall how to do this. Maybe I can break it down into smaller parts to make it easier. \n\nFirst, I know that 77 times 36 is the same as 77 added to itself 36 times, but that sounds like a lot of addition. There must be a smarter way. Oh, right! The distributive property can help here. Maybe I can split 77 into 70 and 7, and 36 into 30 and 6. Wait, actually, maybe splitting one of them would be better. Let me think.\n\nAlternatively, I can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Let me write it down step by step. \n\nSo, writing 77 multiplied by 36. Let me set it up vertically:\n\n\u2003\u00a077  \n\u00d7\u00a036  \n------\n\nStarting with the multiplication by the units digit first. The 6 is in the ones place, so multiply 77 by 6. \n\n77 \u00d7 6: 7 times 6 is 42, and then 70 times 6 is 420. Adding those together gives 420 + 42 = 462. Wait, actually, maybe breaking it down as (70 + 7) \u00d7 6 = 70\u00d76 + 7\u00d76 = 420 + 42 = 462. That's correct.\n\nNow, moving to the tens place. The 3 in 36 is in the tens place, so that's actually 30. So we need to multiply 77 by 30. But since it's the tens place, the result should be shifted one position to the left. Let me compute 77 \u00d7 30. \n\nAgain, breaking it down: 70 \u00d7 30 = 2100, and 7 \u00d7 30 = 210. Adding those gives 2100 + 210 = 2310. Alternatively, 77 \u00d7 3 \u00d7 10 = 231 \u00d7 10 = 2310. Either way, same result.\n\nNow, add the two partial products together: 462 (from the ones place) and 2310 (from the tens place). \n\nAdding them: 462 + 2310. Let's see, 462 + 2000 is 2462, then plus 310 more? Wait, no, 2310 is 2000 + 310. Wait, actually, 2310 is 2000 + 300 + 10. So adding 462 + 2310:\n\nStart with the units: 2 + 0 = 2. Then tens: 6 + 1 = 7. Hundreds: 4 + 3 = 7. Thousands: 0 + 2 = 2. Wait, that gives 2772? Wait, but adding 462 + 2310:\n\nAlternatively, 2310 + 400 is 2710, then +60 is 2770, then +2 is 2772. Yes, that's right. So total is 2772.\n\nHmm, let me check if that's correct. Maybe another way to verify. \n\nAlternatively, using another method: 77 \u00d7 36. Let me see if I can do this mentally or another way. Maybe using the fact that 77 is 70 +7, so 70\u00d736 +7\u00d736. \n\nCalculating 70\u00d736: 7\u00d736=252, so 70\u00d736 is 252\u00d710=2520. \n\nThen 7\u00d736: 7\u00d730=210 and 7\u00d76=42, so 210+42=252. \n\nAdding those together: 2520 +252 = 2772. Same result. Okay, that matches.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property in a different way. Let me try 36 as 30 +6, so 77\u00d7(30+6)=77\u00d730 +77\u00d76, which is the same as before. So that gives 2310 +462=2772. Yep.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using some other trick. Since 77 is 7\u00d711, and 36 is 12\u00d73. Hmm, not sure if that helps. 7\u00d711\u00d712\u00d73. Maybe rearrange: 7\u00d73=21, 11\u00d712=132. Then 21\u00d7132. Let me see if that's easier. 21\u00d7132. \n\n21\u00d7100=2100, 21\u00d730=630, 21\u00d72=42. Adding those: 2100+630=2730, +42=2772. Same answer. So that works too. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the fact that 77\u00d736 = (70+7)\u00d736 =70\u00d736 +7\u00d736. Wait, that's the same as before. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use 36\u00d770 is 2520, and 36\u00d77 is 252. Adding them gives 2772. \n\nAlternatively, maybe approximate. 75\u00d736 is easier? 75\u00d736=2700, since 75\u00d736= (70\u00d736)+(5\u00d736)=2520+180=2700. Then 77\u00d736 is 2 more 36s, so 2700 + 72=2772. That works too. \n\nHmm, so all methods lead to 2772. I think that's the correct answer. Let me just do a quick check with another method. Maybe using calculator-style multiplication:\n\nMultiply 77 by 36:\n\nFirst, 7\u00d76=42, write down 2, carryover 4. \n\nThen 7\u00d73=21, plus the carried over 4 is 25. So first partial product is 252. Wait, but hold on, that's if we are doing 77 \u00d7 6. Wait, maybe I confused the steps. Let me write it again properly.\n\nWait, when multiplying 77 \u00d736:\n\nFirst, multiply 77 by 6 (units digit):\n\n7\u00d76=42, write 2, carryover 4.\n\nThen 7\u00d76 again (the tens digit of 77 is also 7), so 7\u00d76=42 plus the carried over 4 is 46. So the first partial product is 462.\n\nThen multiply 77 by 30 (the 3 in tens place):\n\n7\u00d73=21, write down 1, carryover 2.\n\nThen 7\u00d73 again (the tens digit) is 21 plus 2 is 23. So that gives 231, but since it's the tens place, we shift one position, so it becomes 2310.\n\nAdding 462 +2310=2772. \n\nYes, that's the same as before. So all methods confirm that the product is 2772. I think that's solid. \n\nAlternatively, maybe check with prime factors? Let's see:\n\n77 factors into 7\u00d711.\n\n36 factors into 2\u00b2\u00d73\u00b2.\n\nSo multiplying them together: 7\u00d711\u00d72\u00b2\u00d73\u00b2. \n\nGrouping them as (2\u00b2\u00d73\u00b2) \u00d77\u00d711. \n\n2\u00b2\u00d73\u00b2 is 4\u00d79=36. So 36\u00d77\u00d711. \n\n36\u00d77 is 252, then 252\u00d711. \n\nMultiplying 252\u00d711: 252\u00d710=2520 +252=2772. Yep, same result. \n\nAlright, so all different methods of breaking it down give the same answer, so I'm confident the product of 77 and 36 is 2772.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 77 and 36 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Breakdown using the distributive property:**\n   - Multiply 77 by 6 (units place of 36):\n     \\[\n     77 \\times 6 = 462\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 77 by 30 (tens place of 36, shifted left by one position):\n     \\[\n     77 \\times 30 = 2,\\!310\n     \\]\n   - Add the partial products:\n     \\[\n     462 + 2,\\!310 = 2,\\!772\n     \\]\n\n2. **Verification with alternative methods:**\n   - **Prime factorization:**\n     \\[\n     77 = 7 \\times 11 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 36 = 2^2 \\times 3^2\n     \\]\n     Combining factors:\n     \\[\n     (7 \\times 11) \\times (2^2 \\times 3^2) = (7 \\times 3^2 \\times 2^2) \\times 11 = 252 \\times 11 = 2,\\!772\n     \\]\n   - **Approximation check:**\n     \\[\n     75 \\times 36 = 2,\\!700 \\quad \\text{(base value)}, \\quad \\text{then add } 2 \\times 36 = 72 \\quad \\Rightarrow 2,\\!700 + 72 = 2,\\!772\n     \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 77 and 36 is \\boxed{2772}.",
