earlier. Either way, same answer. Hmm, so I think 1127 is the correct product. Let me just do the multiplication straight up:\n\n49\n×23\n------\nFirst, 3×9=27, write down 7, carryover 2.\n\n3×4=12, plus the 2 is 14. So first line is 147.\n\nThen, since the second digit is 2 (tens place), we start with a zero or shift one position. So 2×9=18, write down 8, carryover 1.\n\n2×4=8, plus 1 is 9. So that gives 980. Then adding 147 and 980 gives 1127. Yep, all methods lead to the same answer. So I think that's solid. Maybe I was just adding wrong when I thought I got 1134 before, but now I see it's 1127. Alright, confident with that.\n"]
