0, then add another 73, so 2920 +73 = 2993. Yeah, that works. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use calculator verification? But since I can't use a calculator, I need to check manually. \n\nLet me add again step by step:\n\n73 * 40:\n\n73 * 4 = 292. So 73 *40 is 2920. Correct.\n\nThen 73*1 =73.\n\nAdding 2920 +73. 2920 +70 is 2990, plus 3 is 2993. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can reverse the numbers. 41*70 is 2870, and 41*3 is 123. Then 2870 + 123 = 2993. Yes, that's another way. 41 times 70 is 2870, plus 41*3=123. 2870 +123: 2870 +100 is 2970, plus 23 is 2993. \n\nOkay, so all methods are giving me 2993. I think that's the correct answer. Maybe I was worried because sometimes when adding up the parts you can make a mistake, but since all different methods give the same result, I can be confident. \n\nWait, let me do one more check. Let's do 73 *41. Let me write it vertically again:\n\n   73\n\nx 41\n\n--------\n\nFirst line: 73*1 =73\n\nSecond line: 73*4 (but shifted one position to the left because it's the tens place). So 73*4 is 292, shifted left becomes 2920.\n\nAdd 73 +2920. \n\n73 +2920. Let's add units digits: 0 +3 =3, then 2 +2=4, 9 +9=18? Wait, maybe breaking down:\n\n2920\n\n+\u00a0 73\n\n------\n\nAdding the units: 0 +3 =3\n\nTens place: 2 +7 =9\n\nHundreds place: 9 + 0 (since 73 has no hundreds) =9\n\nThousands place: 2 remains.\n\nWait, that gives 2993. Yeah, exactly. So that's correct. \n\nI think that's thorough enough. The product is 2993.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 73 and 41 is calculated as follows:\n\nFirst, break down the multiplication using the distributive property:\n\\[\n73 \\times 41 = (70 + 3) \\times (40 + 1)\n\\]\nExpand the terms:\n\\[\n= 70 \\times 40 + 70 \\times 1 + 3 \\times 40 + 3 \\times 1\n\\]\nCalculate each part:\n\\[\n= 2800 + 70 + 120 + 3\n\\]\nAdd the results together:\n\\[\n2800 + 70 = 2870 \\\\\n2870 + 120 = 2990 \\\\\n2990 + 3 = 2993\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** 2993",
