0 is 1560, then 1560 + 120 is 1680, and 1680 + 36 is indeed 1716. \n\nAlternatively, maybe there's another way to check. Maybe I can do 44 times 40, which is 1760, and then subtract 44 from that because 44 times 39 is 44 times (40 -1). So, 44*40 = 1760, minus 44 gives 1760 - 44 = 1716. Yep, same result. That seems to confirm it. \n\nAnother way to verify could be using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   44\nx 39\n------\nFirst multiply 44 by 9: 44*9. Let's see, 40*9=360 and 4*9=36, so 360+36=396.\n\nThen multiply 44 by 30. 44*30 is 44*3*10. 44*3 is 132, so times 10 is 1320.\n\nAdding those two results: 396 + 1320. Let's add them. 396 + 1320. 1320 + 300 is 1620, plus 96 more is 1716. \n\nSame answer again. Okay, so all methods are pointing to 1716. I think that's the correct product. \n\nJust to be thorough, maybe I can use a calculator if I have one, but since I'm doing this manually, the multiple methods all leading to 1716 gives me confidence. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. So, I think the answer is 1716.\n"]
