 Wait, 2730 plus 117. Let me do it step by step. 2730 + 100 is 2830, then +17 is 2847. So the total is 2847?\n\nWait, but let me verify that again because sometimes when I do multiplication step by step, I might make a mistake. Let me try another method to cross-check. Maybe using the distributive property. Breaking down the numbers into smaller components.\n\n39 can be written as 40 - 1, and 73 can be written as 70 + 3. So, (40 - 1)(70 + 3). Let's expand this:\n\nFirst, multiply 40 by 70: that's 2800.\n\nThen 40 times 3 is 120.\n\nThen -1 times 70 is -70.\n\nAnd -1 times 3 is -3.\n\nNow add all those together: 2800 + 120 is 2920. Then subtract 70: 2920 -70 = 2850. Then subtract 3 more: 2850 -3 = 2847. Okay, same answer as before. So that's a good sign.\n\nAlternatively, maybe another way. Let me try 39 times 70 plus 39 times 3. Since 73 is 70 +3. \n\n39 times 70: Well, 39*7 is 273, so times 10 is 2730. Then 39*3 is 117. Adding 2730 +117 is 2847. Yep, same result.\n\nHmm, seems like all methods are giving me 2847, so that's probably the correct answer. But let me just try doing the multiplication again step by step to be thorough.\n\nMultiplying 39 by 73:\n\nFirst, write 39\n\nx73\n\nMultiply 3 (units place) by 39: 3*9=27, write down 7, carryover 2. Then 3*3=9 +2=11. So first partial product is 117.\n\nThen multiply 7 (tens place, so actually 70) by 39. So 7*9=63, write down 3, carryover 6. Then 7*3=21 +6=27. So that's 273, but shifted one position to the left, making it 2730.\n\nAdding 117 +2730: 2730 + 100 =2830, then +17=2847. Yep, same as before.\n\nAlright, so I think the product of 39 and 73 is 2847. I tried three different methods: standard multiplication, distributive property breaking down both numbers, and breaking down one number and using distributive. All led to the same answer. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I'm confident this is correct.\n"]
