 3400 how many times? 40 × 80 is 3200, subtract that from 3400, you get 200. Then 40 goes into 200 five times. So 80 + 5 = 85. That's exactly the other number, so that checks out. \n\nAlternatively, divide 3400 by 85. Let's see, 85 times 40 is the original problem. Let's do 3400 ÷ 85. 85 × 40 is 3400, so that works. \n\nI think that's solid. All the different methods confirm that the product is 3400. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I'm confident that's the right answer.\n"]
