akes here. All the different approaches give the same result, so I'm confident the answer is 1200.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 40 and 30 is calculated by multiplying the two numbers together:\n\n\\[\n40 \\times 30 = (4 \\times 10) \\times (3 \\times 10) = (4 \\times 3) \\times (10 \\times 10) = 12 \\times 100 = 1200\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** 1200",
