1200. That works too.\n\nI think all methods are pointing to 1200. Let me just confirm with a calculator in my mind. 40 multiplied by 30. 4 times 3 is 12, and then two zeros, so 1200. Definitely that's correct. I don't think I made any mistakes here. All the different approaches give the same result, so I'm confident the answer is 1200.\n"]
