tive property breaking into 80+7, breaking into 90-3, standard algorithm, commutative property, and FOIL all give me 3915. So I can be confident that's the correct answer. I think that's thorough enough. Probably overkill, but better safe than sorry.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 45 and 87 is \\boxed{3915}.\n"] 73%|███████▎  | 366/500 [6:27:59<3:30:35, 94.29s/it]
