the products into the grid cells. \n\nSo, 7×1 is 07, 7×3 is 21, 2×1 is 02, and 2×3 is 06. Then, add the diagonals. The first diagonal (from the top right) is just 6. The next diagonal is 1 + 0 + 2 = 3. Then the next is 2 + 0 = 2, and the last is 0. Wait, that gives me 936 when read from top to bottom? Let me see:\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the lattice steps. Let me try again. The lattice method might be confusing me here. Let me think again. Alternatively, maybe I can do the multiplication vertically:\n\n   72\n× 13\n-------\nFirst multiply 72 by 3: that's 216.\nThen multiply 72 by 10 (the 1 in 13 is in the tens place), so that's 720.\nAdd them together: 216 + 720 = 936. Yep, same as before.\n\nHmm, okay, so both methods give me 936. That seems consistent. Let me check with another approach. Maybe breaking down 72 into factors. 72 is 8×9, so 8×9×13. Let's see, 8×13 is 104, then 104×9. 100×9 is 900 and 4×9 is 36, so 900+36=936. Same result. \n\nAlternatively, 13 is 10 + 3, so 72×10 + 72×3 = 720 + 216 = 936. Yep, that's the same as the first method. \n\nI think that's solid. Maybe use a calculator if I had one, but since I'm doing it manually, all the different methods are giving me the same answer, so I can be confident it's correct. \n\nWait, just to be thorough, let me do the multiplication step-by-step the traditional way:\n\n   72\n× 13\n-------\nFirst, write 72 times 3: 216.\nThen, write 72 times 1 (but since it's the tens place, it's actually 10), so shift one position to the left: 720.\nAdd them:\n\n  216\n+720\n-------\n  936\n\nYep, exactly the same. So all methods converge to 936. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. Therefore, the product of 72 and 13 is 936.\n"]
