48:\n\nFirst, write 17\n           x48\n       --------\n           136  (which is 17*8)\n          680   (which is 17*40, shifted one position to the left)\n       --------\n          816\n\nAdding those gives 136 + 680, which is indeed 816. Hmm, that seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another approach. Let's see, 17 is 10 + 7. So, (10 + 7)*48 = 10*48 + 7*48. 10*48 is 480, and 7*48. Let's compute 7*48. 7*40 is 280, and 7*8 is 56, so 280+56 = 336. Adding those together: 480 + 336. 480 + 300 is 780, plus 36 is 816. Same result.\n\nAnother way: Maybe using the fact that 48 is 50 - 2. So, 17*(50 - 2) = 17*50 - 17*2. 17*50 is 850, and 17*2 is 34. So 850 - 34 = 816. Yep, that works too.\n\nHmm, all methods are giving me 816, so I think that's the right answer. Let me just do a quick check with a calculator in my mind. 17 times 50 would be 850, so subtracting two 17s (which is 34) gives 816. Yep, that matches. Alright, I feel confident that the product of 17 and 48 is 816.\n"] 74%|███████▍  | 370/500 [6:31:46<2:19:31, 64.40s/it]
