natively, maybe do it vertically:\n\n   43  \n\u00d772  \n------  \nFirst multiply 43 by 2: 86.\n\nThen multiply 43 by 70 (so shift one position to the left):\n\n43  \n\u00d770  \n-----  \n210 (but since it's 70, actually, 43\u00d77=210? Wait, no. Wait 43\u00d77 is 301, so 43\u00d770 is 3010. So when written vertically, it would be:\n\n     43  \n   \u00d772  \n   ------  \n     86   (43\u00d72)  \n   3010   (43\u00d770, shifted one position to the left)  \n   ------  \n   3096  \n\nYes, adding 86 and 3010 gives 3096. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method, like the lattice method? Hmm, but that might take longer. Alternatively, check using a calculator? But since I can't use a calculator, maybe do another verification. \n\nLet me try adding 43 seventy-two times. Well, that's impractical, but perhaps break it down. \n\nAlternatively, 72 is 70 +2, so 43\u00d770 +43\u00d72, which is exactly what I did before. \n\nAlternatively, reverse the numbers: 72\u00d743. Maybe compute that way. \n\n72 \u00d740 = 2880, and 72 \u00d73=216. Then 2880 +216 = 3096. Yep, same answer. \n\nSo that seems consistent. \n\nWait, just to make sure, let me do 43\u00d772 step by step again. \n\nFirst, write 72 on top and 43 below:\n\n   72  \n\u00d743  \n------  \nMultiply 72 by 3: 216. \n\nMultiply 72 by 40: 72\u00d740. 72\u00d74=288, so 2880. \n\nAdd 216 +2880: 216+2800 is 3016, plus 80 more is 3096. \n\nSame result. \n\nOkay, so all methods are leading me to 3096, so I think that's the correct product. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I'm confident that's the right answer.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 43 and 72 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication using the distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   43 \\times 72 = 43 \\times (70 + 2) = (43 \\times 70) + (43 \\times 2)\n   \\]\n   \n2. **Calculate each part:**\n   - \\( 43 \\times 70 = 3010 \\)\n   - \\( 43 \\times 2 = 86 \\)\n\n3. **Add the results:**\n   \\[\n   3010 + 86 = 3096\n   \\]\n\n**Verification using another method:**\n- Reverse the multiplication (\\(72 \\times 43\\)):\n  - \\( 72 \\times 40 = 2880 \\)\n  - \\( 72 \\times 3 = 216 \\)\n  - \\( 2880 + 216 = 3096 \\)\n\nBoth methods confirm the result is consistent.\n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{3096}\\)",
