Multiply 37 by 80: 2960 (since 37*8=296, then add a zero)  \nAdd them: 74 + 2960 = 3034. \n\nYep, that's the same as before. \n\nAlternatively, if I use a calculator, but since I don't have one here, but given that all manual methods give the same result, I can be confident it's correct. \n\nWait, just to check for any possible arithmetic errors. Let me recompute 37 x8. \n\n37 x8: 30x8=240, 7x8=56, so 240+56=296. Correct. \n\nThen 296 x10 = 2960. \n\n37x2 is 74. \n\nAdding 2960 +74: 2960 +70 is 3030, plus 4 is 3034. \n\nYes, that's right. \n\nAlternatively, maybe check if 3034 divided by 37 gives 82. Let's see:\n\n3034 ÷37. Let's do the division. \n\n37 into 3034. \n\nFirst, how many times does 37 go into 303? \n\n37x8=296, 37x9=333 which is too much. So 8 times. 8x37 is 296. Subtract 296 from 303: 7. Bring down the 4, making 74. \n\n37 goes into 74 exactly 2 times. \n\nSo total is 82. Perfect, that checks out. \n\nTherefore, the product of 37 and 82 is 3034. \n\nI think that's solid. I can't see any mistakes in my calculations, and multiple methods confirm the same result. So I'm confident that's the correct answer.\n"] 75%|███████▌  | 376/500 [6:37:26<2:05:15, 60.60s/it]
