So, 2070 + 345. 2070 + 300 is 2370, plus 45 is 2415. Yep, same answer again.\n\nHmm, seems like all methods are pointing towards 2415. Maybe I should verify with a calculator, but since I can't use one, I'll just check my calculations again.\n\nWait, let me try adding the numbers in another way. If I do 35*69, maybe I can think of 35 as 7*5, and 69 as 7*10 + something? Not sure. Alternatively, 69 is 60+9, so maybe 35*(60+9)=35*60 +35*9. 35*60 is 2100, and 35*9 is 315, so total 2415. Yep, same result again. I think that's solid.\n\nAlternatively, cross-multiplying digits. Let me see:\n\n35\nx69\n------\nFirst multiply 5*9 =45, write 5, carryover 4.\n\nThen 3*9=27 +4=31. So first partial product is 315.\n\nThen, moving to the tens digit (6), we start with a zero or shift one position. So 5*6=30, write 0 and carryover 3. Then 3*6=18 +3=21. So the second partial product is 2100 (since shifted one place). Then adding 315 +2100 gives 2415. Yep, same as before.\n\nI think that's thorough enough. All methods lead to the same answer, so I'm confident it's correct. So the product of 35 and 69 is 2415.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 35 and 69 is \\boxed{2415}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 35 and 69, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy:\n\n1. **Distributive Property (35*(70 - 1))**:\n   \\[\n   35 \\times 69 = 35 \\times (70 - 1) = (35 \\times 70) - (35 \\times 1)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   35 \\times 70 = 2450 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 35 \\times 1 = 35\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2450 - 35 = 2415\n   \\]\n\n2. **Standard Algorithm**:\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     \\quad 35 \\\\\n   \\times 69 \\\\\n   \\hline\n     315 \\quad (\\text{35 \u00d7 9}) \\\\\n   +2100 \\quad (\\text{35 \u00d7 60, shifted one position left}) \\\\\n   \\hline\n     2415 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Distributive Property (30 + 5)**:\n   \\[\n   35 \\times 69 = (30 + 5) \\times 69 = (30 \\times 69) + (5 \\times 69)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   30 \\times 69 = 2070 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 5 \\times 69 = 345\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2070 + 345 = 2415\n   \\]\n\n4. **Alternative Breakdown (60 + 9)**:\n   \\[\n   35 \\times 69 = 35 \\times (60 + 9) = (35 \\times 60) + (35 \\times 9)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   35 \\times 60 = 2100 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 35 \\times 9 = 315\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   2100 + 315 = 2415\n   \\]\n\nAll methods consistently yield the same result. Therefore, the product of 35 and 69 is \\boxed{2415}.",
