00, subtract that from 2790, you get 90 left. 90 goes into 90 once. So 30 +1 =31. Perfect. \n\nOkay, so all the checks confirm that 90 multiplied by 31 is indeed 2790. I think that's solid. No mistakes here. I considered different methods and verified through division. Yep, confident with that answer.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 90 and 31 is calculated by multiplying the two numbers together:\n\n\\[\n90 \\times 31 = 2790\n\\]\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n1. **Breakdown Method:**  \n   - Split 31 into \\(30 + 1\\).  \n   - Multiply \\(90 \\times 30 = 2700\\).  \n   - Multiply \\(90 \\times 1 = 90\\).  \n   - Add the results: \\(2700 + 90 = 2790\\).\n\n2. **Verification via Division:**  \n   - Divide the result by one of the original numbers to check:  \n     \\(2790 \\div 31 = 90\\) (or \\(2790 \\div 90 = 31\\)), confirming the answer is correct.\n\n**Final Answer:**  \n\\[\n\\boxed{2790}\n\\]",
