 10 gives 2790. That works too. \n\nHmm, all the different methods are leading me to 2790. I think that's the right answer. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. Let me just confirm with a calculator maybe? Wait, since I can't use a calculator, but I can do another check. \n\nIf I divide the answer by 31, I should get back to 90. Let's try that. 2790 divided by 31. Let's see: 31 times 90 is... 31*90. Well, 30*90 is 2700, plus 1*90 is 90, so again 2790. So that checks out. \n\nAlternatively, dividing 2790 by 90 should give 31. 2790 divided by 90: 90 goes into 2790 how many times? 90*30 is 2700, subtract that from 2790, you get 90 left. 90 goes into 90 once. So 30 +1 =31. Perfect. \n\nOkay, so all the checks confirm that 90 multiplied by 31 is indeed 2790. I think that's solid. No mistakes here. I considered different methods and verified through division. Yep, confident with that answer.\n"]
