 252. 1960 + 200 is 2160, then add 52 to get 2212. Hmm, but I feel like that might not be correct. Maybe I made a mistake in one of the steps.\n\nLet me verify using another method to be sure. Maybe the standard vertical multiplication:\n\n\u2003\xa028\n×79\n-------\nFirst, multiply 28 by 9 (the units digit of 79):\n28 × 9 = 252. \n\nThen multiply 28 by 70 (the tens digit part, which is 7 in the tens place, so 70):\n28 × 70 = 1960.\n\nNow add those two products: 252 + 1960. Let's see, 252 + 1960. Adding the hundreds: 1900 + 60 = 1960, plus 252. 1960 + 200 is 2160, then +52 is 2212. So that gives the same result. Hmm, so maybe it is 2212?\n\nWait, but let me try another way to cross-verify. Maybe using the distributive property in a different way. Let's see, 28 × 79 can also be written as (30 - 2) × 79. \n\nExpanding that, it's 30×79 - 2×79. Let's compute those:\n\n30 × 79: 30 × 80 is 2400, so subtract 30 to get 2400 - 30 = 2370.\n\nThen 2 × 79 is 158. \n\nSo subtracting: 2370 - 158 = ?\n\n2370 minus 100 is 2270, minus 58 more is 2212. Okay, so that also gives 2212. Hmm, so that matches the previous result. \n\nAlternatively, maybe do 79 × 28 by breaking down 28 into 20 + 8. Let's try that:\n\n79 × 20 = 1580.\n\n79 × 8 = 632. \n\nAdding those together: 1580 + 632. Let's see: 1500 + 600 = 2100, 80 +32 = 112. So total is 2100 + 112 = 2212. \n\nSame answer again. Hmm, so maybe 2212 is correct. But I want to be absolutely sure. Let me try another approach, perhaps the lattice method or using a calculator-like step-by-step.\n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 28 × 80 first, then subtract 28. Because 79 is one less than 80. \n\n28 × 80: 28 × 8 = 224, so times 10 is 2240. \n\nThen subtract 28: 2240 - 28 = 2212. \n\nSame result again. So all methods are pointing towards 2212. \n\nWait, but just to make sure I didn't make a mistake in any of the intermediate steps. Let me check each calculation again:\n\nFirst method:\n\n28 × 70 = 1960 (since 28×7=196, then ×10)\n28 × 9 = 252 (28×10=280 minus 28 gives 252)\n1960 + 252: 1960 + 200 is 2160, plus 52 is 2212. Correct.\n\nSecond method:\n\n(30 -2)×79 = 30×79 -2×79\n30×79: 30×70=2100, 30×9=270, so total 2100+270=2370. Then 2×79=158. 2370-158=2212. Correct.\n\nThird method:\n\n79×20=1580, 79×8=632. 1580+632=2212. Correct.\n\nFourth method:\n\n28×80=2240, minus 28 gives 2212. Correct.\n\nAll methods lead to 2212, so I think that must be the correct product. I don't see any errors in my calculations now. So the answer should be 2212.\n"]
