150; 500+150=650), and 13*10 is 130. Adding those together, 650 +130 = 780. Yep, same answer again. \n\nAlright, I think I'm confident that the product of 13 and 60 is 780. All the different methods cross-check to the same result, so I don't think I made an error here. Probably that's the correct answer.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 13 and 60 is calculated by multiplying the two numbers together. \n\n\\[\n13 \\times 60 = 13 \\times (6 \\times 10) = (13 \\times 6) \\times 10 = 78 \\times 10 = 780\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** 780",
