's see. 16 is 2^4, and 49 is 7^2. So multiplying them together gives 2^4 *7^2. Calculating that: 16*49, which is the same as (2^4)*(7^2). But numerically, 2^4 is 16, 7^2 is 49, so 16*49=784. That checks out too. \n\nWait, maybe I can use another approach, like the difference of squares? Let me think. 16 times 49... Hmm, not sure if that applies here. Maybe if I can express it as (something squared minus something else squared?), but that might complicate things. Probably better to stick with the straightforward methods I already used. \n\nAlternatively, breaking down 16 into 8*2. So 8*2*49. 8*49 is 392, then times 2 is 784. Yep, that works too. \n\nAnother way: 49 is 7 squared, so 16*7 is 112, then times 7 again. 112*7. Let's see, 100*7 is 700, 12*7 is 84, so 700+84=784. That also works. \n\nOkay, so all these different methods are leading me to 784. I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations. Maybe I can use a calculator to confirm, but since I don't have one here, but since multiple manual methods all give the same result, I can be confident it's correct. \n\nWait, just to make sure, let me try adding 49 sixteen times. That's tedious, but maybe do it in parts. 49+49=98 (2), 98+49=147 (3), 147+49=196 (4), 196+49=245 (5), 245+49=294 (6), 294+49=343 (7), 343+49=392 (8), 392+49=441 (9), 441+49=490 (10), 490+49=539 (11), 539+49=588 (12), 588+49=637 (13), 637+49=686 (14), 686+49=735 (15), 735+49=784 (16). Wow, that took a while, but after 16 times, it's 784. That matches. \n\nAlright, so every method I try gives me 784. Definitely the right answer.\n"]
