t. Alright, so the product is 2546.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 67 and 38 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Break down using the standard algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 67 by 8 (units place):\n     ```\n      67  \n    \u00d7  38  \n    \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500  \n     536   (67 \u00d7 8)\n     ```\n   - Multiply 67 by 30 (tens place, shifted left):\n     ```\n      67  \n    \u00d7  38  \n    \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500  \n    2010   (67 \u00d7 30)\n    \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500  \n     ```\n   - Add the partial products:\n     ```\n       536  \n     +2010  \n     \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500  \n      2546  \n     ```\n\n2. **Verification via distributive property:**\n   - Expand \\((60 + 7)(30 + 8)\\):\n     ```\n     60\u00d730 = 1800  \n     60\u00d78 = 480  \n     7\u00d730 = 210  \n     7\u00d78 = 56  \n     ```\n   - Sum the terms:\n     ```\n     1800 + 480 + 210 + 56 = 2546  \n     ```\n\n3. **Alternative method using subtraction:**\n   - Rewrite \\(38\\) as \\(40 - 2\\):\n     ```\n     67\u00d740 = 2680  \n     67\u00d72 = 134  \n     2680 - 134 = 2546  \n     ```\n\n**Final Answer:** The product of 67 and 38 is \\boxed{2546}.",
