that way as another check.\n\n81\u00d740: 81\u00d74=324, so 324\u00d710=3240. \n\n81\u00d74=324. \n\nAdding them gives 3240 +324= 3564. \n\nSame answer again. Okay, so that's three different methods all leading to 3564. Seems solid. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use calculator verification? But since I can't use a calculator, perhaps divide the answer by one of the numbers to see if I get the other. \n\n3564 divided by 81. Let's see. 81\u00d740=3240. 3564-3240=324. Then 324 divided by 81 is 4. So total is 40+4=44. Perfect, that's the other number. So that checks out. \n\nAlternatively, 3564 divided by 44. Let's see. 44\u00d780=3520. 3564-3520=44. So that's 80 +1=81. So that also checks out. \n\nOkay, so all the division checks work. Therefore, I can be confident the product is 3564. \n\nI think that's thorough. Maybe overkill, but better safe than sorry. So the answer is 3564.\n</think>\n\nThe product of 81 and 44 can be calculated using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n81 \\times 44 = (80 + 1) \\times 44 = 80 \\times 44 + 1 \\times 44\n\\]\n\nFirst, compute \\(80 \\times 44\\):\n\\[\n80 \\times 44 = 8 \\times 10 \\times 44 = 8 \\times (10 \\times 44) = 8 \\times 440 = 3,\\!520\n\\]\n\nThen, compute \\(1 \\times 44\\):\n\\[\n1 \\times 44 = 44\n\\]\n\nAdd the results together:\n\\[\n3,\\!520 + 44 = 3,\\!564\n\\]\n\n**Verification**:\n- Dividing the result by 81:  \n  \\(3,\\!564 \\div 81 = 44\\), which matches the original factor.\n- Dividing the result by 44:  \n  \\(3,\\!564 \\div 44 = 81\\), which also matches the original factor.\n\nThus, the product of 81 and 44 is \\(\\boxed{3564}\\).",
